INT. SINKING FISHING TRAWLER, WHEELHOUSE - NIGHT

Water ankle-deep and rising. A lantern swings from the ceiling. Waves slam the hull.

CAPTAIN RUTH ABERNATHY-KOMA (50s, oilskins, grey braid) grips the wheel. Her knuckles are white.

Beside her, deckhand BASTIEN LEFEBVRE-ADEOLA (20s, hood, cut lip) bails with a plastic bucket.

At the radio, first mate MAEVE ONWUACHI-DRUMM (30s, hands taped, glasses fogged) clutches the handset.

MAEVE
(into radio)
Mayday, mayday, this is trawler Gallant Heron, taking water, request assistance.

COAST GUARD (V.O.)
(garbled)
Gallant Heron, say again your position.

MAEVE
Forty-one north, sixty-eight west! Forty-one north!

BASTIEN
How much time?

RUTH
Twenty minutes.

BASTIEN
That's not time. That's a prayer.

COAST GUARD (V.O.)
...ant Heron... one hour... response...

MAEVE
One hour! We don't have one hour!

RUTH
Maeve. Give me the mic.

MAEVE
They can't hear--

RUTH
Give it to me!

Maeve hands it over. A wave rocks the boat. The lantern swings.

RUTH (CONT'D)
(into radio)
Coast Guard, this is Ruth Abernathy. Last transmission. We are abandoning ship in ten minutes. Three souls. Please mark our position.

BASTIEN
Abandoning to what?

RUTH
The raft.

BASTIEN
The raft's been in the shed since March.

RUTH
Then it's had a long rest.

MAEVE
Captain, the pump's dead!

BASTIEN
I'm bailing!

RUTH
Bail faster!

COAST GUARD (V.O.)
...Heron... flare... fire flare...

MAEVE
Flare! Where's the flare?

BASTIEN
Port locker!

MAEVE
It's underwater!

RUTH
Then swim!

Maeve dives into the dark water pooled in the corner. Surfaces gasping. A bright orange flare in her fist.

MAEVE
Got it!

RUTH
Up top! Go!

They push through the hatch. The sea comes at them in sheets. Wind grabs the flare, strikes it. Red fire stabs the sky.

Far off, a searchlight swings. Bastien whoops.

BASTIEN
They see us! They see us!

RUTH
(to herself)
Slow down, Ruth. Don't thank anyone yet.

The hull groans. A wave lifts them. The searchlight finds their faces.
